    "body": "@mikewest Oh, further up being further down. Curse your (well, @bzbarsky 's) Australian terminology.\n\nI suspect it's https://code.google.com/p/chromium/codesearch#chromium/src/components/mime_util/mime_util.cc&l=157 (and the related mime_util) component, which serves a variety of purposes in Blink, and which is not really ideally integrated in with the embedding stack (especially with respect to handling and plugins). Consider all of those functions as full of dragons :)\n\nAs it stands, that function is used by the NavigationController - https://code.google.com/p/chromium/codesearch#chromium/src/content/browser/frame_host/navigation_controller_impl.cc&l=493 - so I suspect whatever it is you're wondering about mime types in places other than Blink, it'll be the mime_util component (and those that depend on it)\n\nIt used to be part of //net, but I moved it out, but really it's more a function of the Blink embedder; we already see the 'weirdness' surface when you compare the html_viewer/Mandoline behaviours when embedding Blink vs when //content embeds Blink, so it's no doubt the wrong model to standardize on :)\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
